  "behavior": [
    "After the original In Documents row Open/back/linkedRows check, the detour selects the unique English Notes segment under the real torah-inspector-tools segmented control.",
    "It requires the actual Notes Add control but does not tap it. The row predicate expressly excludes torah-inspector-note-unlink- from torah-inspector-note- matching.",
    "It waits for and requires one actual row in this fresh-origin fixture, derives a nonempty observed association ID, and then re-queries that complete identifier with unique/enabled/hittable checks. No related-result, fixture-target, account or object identity is substituted for the association ID.",
    "Before tapping the row it attaches actual row identity/count/selected-tool values in a separately named JSON and calls the original AX/screenshot helper.",
    "The row is tapped; original requireCurrentDocument(noteID) and requireBody(editedBlockID,bodyText) bind the production association-resolution route to the Note already created and edited by the journey.",
    "Original nativeBack and openRelatedDocuments return to the origin; linkedRows is rechecked before the untouched original unlink block and every original cold-reopen/body-retention assertion."
  ],
